This license covers the skills in `skills/`, the agent in `agents/`, the
registry, and the installer.

Skills reached through `registry/skills.json` are NOT covered: they are fetched
at install time from their authors' repositories and remain under those
authors' own licenses.

THIRD-PARTY DERIVATIVE WORK

Derived from https://github.com/mattpocock/skills, MIT (c) 2026 Matt Pocock:

    skills/swift-tdd/               <- engineering/tdd
    skills/swift-diagnosing-bugs/   <- engineering/diagnosing-bugs
    skills/swift-code-review/       <- engineering/code-review
    skills/swift-domain-modeling/   <- engineering/domain-modeling
    skills/xcode-merge-conflicts/   <- engineering/resolving-merge-conflicts
    skills/apple-docs-research/     <- engineering/research
    skills/swift-pre-commit/        <- misc/setup-pre-commit

Derived from https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills, MIT (c) 2025 Thomas Ricouard:

    skills/app-store-changelog/
    skills/ios-debugger-agent/
    skills/swift-concurrency-expert/
    skills/swiftui-liquid-glass/
    skills/swiftui-performance-audit/
    skills/swiftui-view-refactor/

Each contains a NOTICE.md reproducing the upstream copyright and permission
notice as those licenses require. The NOTICE ships inside each skill directory
so it travels with any copy the installer makes.

The Ricouard-derived skills were inherited into this repo from local project
copies whose provenance was not recorded at the time. They diverged from
upstream before this repo existed and are NOT a current mirror; see
Dimillian/Skills for the maintained versions.

Original work in this repo:

    skills/apple-foundation-models/
    skills/instruments-profile-session/
    skills/gh-issue-fix-flow/        (provenance unverified; no upstream found)
    agents/, registry/, install.sh, scripts/
